USC: don't move an index register write into a pack on vec34

When the temporary copied into an index register was made by a U16U16 (or
S16S8, U16U8) unpack, the index register became the unpack's destination,
which on a vector core expands to a VPCK for each half of the register.
The index register can't be written a half at a time and the VPCK of the
upper half (with 0) overwrote the index, so a program-scope __constant
int array indexed at run time always read its first element.  Keep the
move, which is encoded as a whole-register IMA16.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/indexreg.c b/tools/intern/usc2/indexreg.c
index 6795b48..6a158b7 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/indexreg.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/indexreg.c
@@ -3135,6 +3135,22 @@ IMG_VOID FoldIndexRegisterWrite(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE psState, PINST psIndexMoveIn
 		return;
 	}
 
+	#if defined(SUPPORT_SGX543) || defined(SUPPORT_SGX544) || defined(SUPPORT_SGX554)
+	/*
+		On a vector core these become a VPCK per half of the destination, and
+		the index register can't be written a half at a time: the second VPCK
+		writes over the first.
+	*/
+	if ((psState->psTargetFeatures->ui32Flags & SGX_FEATURE_FLAGS_USE_VEC34) != 0 &&
+		(psMovSrcDefInst->eOpcode == IUNPCKU16U16 ||
+		 psMovSrcDefInst->eOpcode == IUNPCKS16S8 ||
+		 psMovSrcDefInst->eOpcode == IUNPCKU16U8 ||
+		 (g_psInstDesc[psMovSrcDefInst->eOpcode].uFlags & DESC_FLAGS_VECTORDEST) != 0))
+	{
+		return;
+	}
+	#endif /* defined(SUPPORT_SGX543) || defined(SUPPORT_SGX544) || defined(SUPPORT_SGX554) */
+
 	/*
 		Check the defining instruction doesn't partially define the move source.
 	*/
